@@ -70,6 +70,16 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts its positional objects to strings with normal string conversion, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result followed by ``end``.
+
+Unlike print and log, ``out`` does not pretty print, wrap, crop, apply markup, or replace emoji codes. Text is written as-is. It does apply highlighting by default (set ``highlight=False`` to turn it off) and accepts a basic ``style`` argument, which is applied the same way print applies it::
+
+    >>> console.out("foo", [1, 2, 3], sep=" | ", style="bold")
+
+
